00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:11.120
keeps popping up in today's stories. How AI can pick up hidden biases from the data it learns from

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.060
and sometimes show them in surprising ways. Think of the AI like a student who has read every book,

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:21.420
watched every video and scrolled every social media feed in the world. That student does not get told

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.340
what is right or wrong. It just notices patterns. If most old commercials show boys as pirates and

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.280
ninjas and spies, then the student starts to expect that pattern every time. When you give it a new prompt,

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.240
it reaches for the patterns it knows best. That is basically what happened when two different video

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:41.640
making AIs were given the exact same innocent prompt about a 90s style toy commercial with kids

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:47.700
in Halloween costumes. Both created videos with zero girls, a black boy as the pirate and East Asian

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.920
boy as the ninja, and a white boy as the spy. The creator did not expect those strong racial

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:58.460
and gender patterns and called it enlightening so the AI is not being mean on purpose. It is simply

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:03.440
repeating the world it was shown during training and that is basically how bias sneaks into AI.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.300
Not so scary once you see the pattern matching machine under the hood, right?

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.940
All right, let's talk about some cool stuff you can try today. First up, those same AI video

